cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Knowing the Graph: Does Relational Structure Improve Linear-Probe Detection of Related AI-Safety Concepts?"
abstract: >-
  A four-iteration, pre-registered study of whether relational (graph) structure
  between concepts improves linear-probe detection of related AI-safety concepts
  in the residual stream of Gemma-2-9B, independently peer-replicated on
  Gemma-4-E4B. Finding: relations help only as local hard-negative contrast
  (~0.06 F1, ~1/3 lexical); the graph's connectivity adds no measurable benefit
  at any data volume tested (a powered, pre-registered null on the alternate-path
  / Menger prediction).
